{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWZEYvkeNdbz8HJ9CrRR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019HQgSKBBpAvmb2ogGCbb6N","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/BLAST_RADIUS.md","content":"# CVE Blast Radius Analysis: HTTP/2 Rapid Reset in `golang.org/x/net`\n\n## 1. CVE Identification\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| CVE | **CVE-2023-39325** (Go advisory GO-2023-2102 / GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3) |\n| Industry-wide counterpart | CVE-2023-44487 (\"HTTP/2 Rapid Reset\") |\n| Affected module | `golang.org/x/net` (package `golang.org/x/net/http2`) |\n| Affected versions | `< v0.17.0` |\n| Fixed version | `v0.17.0` |\n| Mechanism | A malicious client can rapidly open and immediately (RST_STREAM) cancel HTTP/2 streams. The server does work to set up/tear down each stream before enforcing `MaxConcurrentStreams`, allowing unbounded resource consumption → denial of service. |\n| Related fixes in the ecosystem | `google.golang.org/grpc` (which vendors/uses `x/net/http2` semantics for its own HTTP/2-based transport) shipped mitigations in v1.56.3 / v1.57.1 / v1.58.3; Go standard library `net/http` (which also implements HTTP/2 via `x/net/http2`-derived code) was patched in Go 1.20.10 / 1.21.3. |\n\n## 2. Repositories Assessed\n\nWorkspace contains three CNCF repos: `/workspace/etcd`, `/workspace/grpc-go`, `/workspace/kubernetes`.\n\n## 3. Direct Dependents — `go.mod` findings\n\n### `/workspace/etcd` (multi-module repo, 8 go.mod files)\n\n| Module (go.mod) | `golang.org/x/net` requirement | Direct/Indirect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/etcd/go.mod` (`go.etcd.io/etcd/v3`) | `v0.7.0` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/api/go.mod` (`go.etcd.io/etcd/api/v3`) | `v0.0.0-20210405180319-a5a99cb37ef4` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/etcdctl/go.mod` | `v0.7.0` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/etcdutl/go.mod` | `v0.7.0` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/pkg/go.mod` | `v0.0.0-20200822124328-c89045814202` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/raft/go.mod` | not required (no direct/indirect entry) | n/a |\n| `/workspace/etcd/server/go.mod` | `v0.7.0` | **direct** |\n| `/workspace/etcd/tests/go.mod` | `v0.7.0` | indirect |\n\nEven though most modules list `x/net` as \"indirect\" in `go.mod`, etcd code **directly imports** `golang.org/x/net/http2` (not just via grpc) in:\n- `/workspace/etcd/client/pkg/transport/listener.go`\n- `/workspace/etcd/server/etcdmain/grpc_proxy.go`\n- `/workspace/etcd/server/embed/serve.go` (embedded etcd server HTTP/gRPC listener setup)\n- `/workspace/etcd/server/proxy/httpproxy/proxy.go`\n\n`google.golang.org/grpc` is required directly at `v1.41.0` in `/workspace/etcd/go.mod`, `/workspace/etcd/server/go.mod`, `/workspace/etcd/etcdctl/go.mod`, `/workspace/etcd/tests/go.mod` — this is the second (transitive) path to `x/net/http2`.\n\n### `/workspace/grpc-go` (2 go.mod files)\n\n| Module (go.mod) | `golang.org/x/net` requirement | Direct/Indirect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/grpc-go/go.mod` (`google.golang.org/grpc`) | `v0.12.0` | **direct** |\n| `/workspace/grpc-go/examples/go.mod` | `v0.12.0` | indirect |\n\n`x/net/http2` (and `http2/hpack`) is imported directly by grpc-go's transport layer:\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/http2_server.go`\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/http2_client.go`\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/http_util.go`\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/controlbuf.go`\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/handler_server.go`\n\nThis is the root of the HTTP/2 attack surface for every gRPC server/client built on this module — grpc-go's own HTTP/2 framing for streams RST is implemented on top of `x/net/http2`, making it the origin of the Rapid Reset exposure for all downstream consumers.\n\n### `/workspace/kubernetes` (single go.mod, vendored)\n\n| Module (go.mod) | `golang.org/x/net` requirement | Direct/Indirect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/kubernetes/go.mod` (`k8s.io/kubernetes`) | `v0.13.0` | **direct** |\n\n`google.golang.org/grpc` is required directly at `v1.54.0` (`/workspace/kubernetes/go.mod` line 91).\n\nKubernetes vendors `x/net/http2` (see `/workspace/kubernetes/vendor/modules.txt` line 972-981, `# golang.org/x/net v0.13.0`) and the **kube-apiserver directly wires up `x/net/http2` for its main secure HTTP/2 listener**:\n- `/workspace/kubernetes/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/secure_serving.go` — imports `golang.org/x/net/http2` and calls `http2.ConfigureServer(secureServer, http2Options)` to configure the HTTP/2 server used by every kube-apiserver instance. This is the primary Rapid-Reset attack surface for Kubernetes clusters (an unauthenticated or authenticated client opening a raw HTTP/2 connection to the API server).\n- Related mitigation-adjacent code already present: `/workspace/kubernetes/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/filters/goaway_test.go` (GOAWAY filter, a separate connection-cycling mitigation, not a fix for Rapid Reset itself).\n\n## 4. Transitive Dependency DAG\n\n```\ngolang.org/x/net/http2  (CVE-2023-39325 origin)\n│\n├── (A) google.golang.org/grpc  [grpc-go, direct dep on x/net v0.12.0]\n│        │\n│        ├── go.etcd.io/etcd/server/v3   (etcd client <-> server, peer <-> peer Raft-over-gRPC, grpc-proxy)\n│        │     requires google.golang.org/grpc v1.41.0  (etcd/go.mod, etcd/server/go.mod)\n│        │\n│        └── k8s.io/kubernetes           (kube-apiserver <-> etcd storage client, KMS plugin gRPC,\n│              requires google.golang.org/grpc v1.54.0    CRI/kubelet plugin gRPC, DRA plugin gRPC)\n│              (kubernetes/go.mod line 91; see e.g.\n│               /workspace/kubernetes/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/storage/storagebackend/factory/etcd3.go,\n│               /workspace/kubernetes/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/storage/value/encrypt/envelope/grpc_service.go,\n│               /workspace/kubernetes/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/storage/value/encrypt/envelope/kmsv2/grpc_service.go,\n│               /workspace/kubernetes/staging/src/k8s.io/cri-api/pkg/apis/runtime/v1/api.pb.go)\n│\n├── (B) go.etcd.io/etcd  (direct import of x/net/http2, independent of grpc-go)\n│        - client/pkg/transport/listener.go   (TLS+HTTP/2 listener for client traffic)\n│        - server/embed/serve.go              (embedded server's HTTP/2-enabled listener)\n│        - server/etcdmain/grpc_proxy.go      (grpc-proxy's own HTTP/2 handling)\n│        - server/proxy/httpproxy/proxy.go    (HTTP reverse proxy)\n│\n└── (C) k8s.io/kubernetes  (direct import of x/net/http2, independent of grpc-go)\n         - staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/secure_serving.go\n           (kube-apiserver's primary secure HTTP/2 listener — configures http2.Server directly)\n```\n\n**Key finding:** Kubernetes and etcd are each exposed via **two independent paths** — (1) directly importing `x/net/http2` for their own HTTP servers/listeners, and (2) transitively via `google.golang.org/grpc`'s HTTP/2 transport. Patching only the direct `x/net` dependency is not sufficient; the `google.golang.org/grpc` version pinned by each repo must also carry (or be upgraded to carry) the corresponding grpc-side Rapid Reset mitigation, since grpc-go implements its own stream/settings bookkeeping around `x/net/http2` framing.\n\n## 5. Version Analysis — Resolved (`go.sum`) vs. Fixed (`v0.17.0`)\n\n\"Resolved version\" = the `h1:`-hashed (actually-downloaded/built) version in the leaf `go.sum`, which is the version Go's module graph (MVS) will actually compile in — this can differ from what a `go.mod` merely lists as a lower bound.\n\n| Repo | go.mod path | Resolved `x/net` version (go.sum `h1:` entry) | Before/after `v0.17.0`? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| etcd | `/workspace/etcd/go.sum` | `v0.7.0` | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n| etcd | `/workspace/etcd/api/go.sum` | `v0.0.0-20210405180319-a5a99cb37ef4` | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n| etcd | `/workspace/etcd/etcdctl/go.sum` | `v0.7.0` | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n| etcd | `/workspace/etcd/etcdutl/go.sum` | `v0.7.0` | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n| etcd | `/workspace/etcd/pkg/go.sum` | `v0.0.0-20200822124328-c89045814202` | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n| etcd | `/workspace/etcd/raft/go.sum` | no `h1:` (build-list only, unused) | n/a |\n| etcd | `/workspace/etcd/server/go.sum` | `v0.7.0` | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n| etcd | `/workspace/etcd/tests/go.sum` | `v0.7.0` | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n| grpc-go | `/workspace/grpc-go/go.sum` | `v0.12.0` | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n| grpc-go | `/workspace/grpc-go/examples/go.sum` | `v0.12.0` | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n| kubernetes | `/workspace/kubernetes/go.sum` | `v0.13.0` (also pinned in `/workspace/kubernetes/vendor/modules.txt`) | **Before — VULNERABLE** |\n\n**All three repositories, across every module examined, resolve to a `golang.org/x/net` version older than the `v0.17.0` fix.** etcd's `api` and `pkg` submodules are furthest behind, still on pre-release pseudo-versions from 2020/2021.\n\n## 6. Blast Radius Summary\n\n| Repo | Exposed component(s) | Attack surface | Direct `x/net` exposure | Transitive (via grpc-go) exposure |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **kubernetes** | kube-apiserver (`secure_serving.go`), etcd storage client, KMS gRPC plugins, CRI/kubelet/DRA gRPC plugins | Highest — kube-apiserver's main client-facing HTTPS/HTTP2 listener is directly built on the vulnerable package; an attacker with network access to the API server port can trigger resource exhaustion | Yes (direct) | Yes (grpc v1.54.0) |\n| **etcd** | client listener, embedded server listener, grpc-proxy, HTTP reverse proxy, Raft/client gRPC | High — etcd's client and peer endpoints are HTTP/2-capable; grpc-proxy and httpproxy add extra direct exposure | Yes (direct, 4 call sites) | Yes (grpc v1.41.0) |\n| **grpc-go** | Core HTTP/2 transport (`internal/transport/http2_*.go`) | Origin of the transitive risk for every consumer — any service built on this grpc-go version is exposed | Yes (direct, root cause for path A) | n/a (is the transport) |\n\n## 7. Remediation Notes (for coordination, not applied here)\n\n- Bump `golang.org/x/net` to `>= v0.17.0` in every `go.mod`/`go.sum` listed in §5 (etcd has 7 independent modules to update; kubernetes additionally requires `go mod vendor` to refresh `vendor/golang.org/x/net` and `vendor/modules.txt`).\n- Bump `google.golang.org/grpc` in etcd (`v1.41.0`) and kubernetes (`v1.54.0`) to a patched line (`>= v1.56.3`, `>= v1.57.1`, or `>= v1.58.3`) to close path (A) — bumping `x/net` alone does not patch grpc-go's own stream-accounting mitigations.\n- After bumping, re-run `go mod tidy`/`go mod vendor` in each module and re-verify `go.sum` resolves to `>= v0.17.0` for `x/net` in all leaf modules (etcd's multi-module layout means each of the 8 `go.mod` files must be checked independently — a fix in the root module does not propagate to `api`, `pkg`, `etcdctl`, `etcdutl`, or `tests` submodules automatically).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63454,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":49,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e1ae515-aa8a-48a6-9867-4650db0a9b6d","uuid":"0e184c57-b55d-4836-8a50-0b1244398944","timestamp":"2026-07-29T15:07:10.012Z","request_id":"req_011CdWZEXSxgPMGuaDqcwNh2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019HQgSKBBpAvmb2ogGCbb6N","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /workspace/BLAST_RADIUS.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e1ae515-aa8a-48a6-9867-4650db0a9b6d","uuid":"a925ce51-80d4-4ae2-bdfd-4266e19bc3db","timestamp":"2026-07-29T15:07:10.021Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/workspace/BLAST_RADIUS.md","content":"# CVE Blast Radius Analysis: HTTP/2 Rapid Reset in `golang.org/x/net`\n\n## 1. CVE Identification\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| CVE | **CVE-2023-39325** (Go advisory GO-2023-2102 / GHSA-qppj-fm5r-hxr3) |\n| Industry-wide counterpart | CVE-2023-44487 (\"HTTP/2 Rapid Reset\") |\n| Affected module | `golang.org/x/net` (package `golang.org/x/net/http2`) |\n| Affected versions | `< v0.17.0` |\n| Fixed version | `v0.17.0` |\n| Mechanism | A malicious client can rapidly open and immediately (RST_STREAM) cancel HTTP/2 streams. The server does work to set up/tear down each stream before enforcing `MaxConcurrentStreams`, allowing unbounded resource consumption → denial of service. |\n| Related fixes in the ecosystem | `google.golang.org/grpc` (which vendors/uses `x/net/http2` semantics for its own HTTP/2-based transport) shipped mitigations in v1.56.3 / v1.57.1 / v1.58.3; Go standard library `net/http` (which also implements HTTP/2 via `x/net/http2`-derived code) was patched in Go 1.20.10 / 1.21.3. |\n\n## 2. Repositories Assessed\n\nWorkspace contains three CNCF repos: `/workspace/etcd`, `/workspace/grpc-go`, `/workspace/kubernetes`.\n\n## 3. Direct Dependents — `go.mod` findings\n\n### `/workspace/etcd` (multi-module repo, 8 go.mod files)\n\n| Module (go.mod) | `golang.org/x/net` requirement | Direct/Indirect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/etcd/go.mod` (`go.etcd.io/etcd/v3`) | `v0.7.0` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/api/go.mod` (`go.etcd.io/etcd/api/v3`) | `v0.0.0-20210405180319-a5a99cb37ef4` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/etcdctl/go.mod` | `v0.7.0` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/etcdutl/go.mod` | `v0.7.0` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/pkg/go.mod` | `v0.0.0-20200822124328-c89045814202` | indirect |\n| `/workspace/etcd/raft/go.mod` | not required (no direct/indirect entry) | n/a |\n| `/workspace/etcd/server/go.mod` | `v0.7.0` | **direct** |\n| `/workspace/etcd/tests/go.mod` | `v0.7.0` | indirect |\n\nEven though most modules list `x/net` as \"indirect\" in `go.mod`, etcd code **directly imports** `golang.org/x/net/http2` (not just via grpc) in:\n- `/workspace/etcd/client/pkg/transport/listener.go`\n- `/workspace/etcd/server/etcdmain/grpc_proxy.go`\n- `/workspace/etcd/server/embed/serve.go` (embedded etcd server HTTP/gRPC listener setup)\n- `/workspace/etcd/server/proxy/httpproxy/proxy.go`\n\n`google.golang.org/grpc` is required directly at `v1.41.0` in `/workspace/etcd/go.mod`, `/workspace/etcd/server/go.mod`, `/workspace/etcd/etcdctl/go.mod`, `/workspace/etcd/tests/go.mod` — this is the second (transitive) path to `x/net/http2`.\n\n### `/workspace/grpc-go` (2 go.mod files)\n\n| Module (go.mod) | `golang.org/x/net` requirement | Direct/Indirect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/grpc-go/go.mod` (`google.golang.org/grpc`) | `v0.12.0` | **direct** |\n| `/workspace/grpc-go/examples/go.mod` | `v0.12.0` | indirect |\n\n`x/net/http2` (and `http2/hpack`) is imported directly by grpc-go's transport layer:\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/http2_server.go`\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/http2_client.go`\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/http_util.go`\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/controlbuf.go`\n- `/workspace/grpc-go/internal/transport/handler_server.go`\n\nThis is the root of the HTTP/2 attack surface for every gRPC server/client built on this module — grpc-go's own HTTP/2 framing for streams RST is implemented on top of `x/net/http2`, making it the origin of the Rapid Reset exposure for all downstream consumers.\n\n### `/workspace/kubernetes` (single go.mod, vendored)\n\n| Module (go.mod) | `golang.org/x/net` requirement | Direct/Indirect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/kubernetes/go.mod` (`k8s.io/kubernetes`) | `v0.13.0` | **direct** |\n\n`google.golang.org/grpc` is required directly at `v1.54.0` (`/workspace/kubernetes/go.mod` line 91).\n\nKubernetes vendors `x/net/http2` (see `/workspace/kubernetes/vendor/modules.txt` line 972-981, `# golang.org/x/net v0.13.0`) and the **kube-apiserver directly wires up `x/net/http2` for its main secure HTTP/2 listener**:\n- `/workspace/kubernetes/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/secure_serving.go` — imports `golang.org/x/net/http2` and calls `http2.ConfigureServer(secureServer, http2Options)` to configure the HTTP/2 server used by every kube-apiserver instance. This is the primary Rapid-Reset attack surface for Kubernetes clusters (an unauthenticated or authenticated client opening a raw HTTP/2 connection to the API server).\n- Related mitigation-adjacent code already present: `/workspace/kubernetes/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/filters/goaway_test.go` (GOAWAY filter, a separate connection-cycling mitigation, not a fix for Rapid Reset itself).\n\n## 4. Transitive Dependency DAG\n\n```\ngolang.org/x/net/http2  (CVE-2023-39325 origin)\n│\n├── (A) google.golang.org/grpc  [grpc-go, direct dep on x/net v0.12.0]\n│        │\n│        ├── go.etcd.io/etcd/server/v3   (etcd client <-> server, peer <-> peer Raft-over-gRPC, grpc-proxy)\n│        │     requires google.golang.org/grpc v1.41.0  (etcd/go.mod, etcd/server/go.mod)\n│        │\n│        └── k8s.io/kubernetes           (kube-apiserver <-> etcd storage client, KMS plugin gRPC,\n│              requires google.golang.org/grpc v1.54.0    CRI/kubelet plugin gRPC, DRA plugin gRPC)\n│              (kubernetes/go.mod line 91; see e.g.\n│               /workspace/kubernetes/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/storage/storagebackend/factory/etcd3.go,\n│              